    "summary": "A tight, beat-locked motion-graphics edit: hard cuts every 0.7-1.5s landing on a ~120 BPM percussion track, one white flash-frame punctuation, continuous push/pull camera moves inside every shot, and fully saturated synthetic color fields. The core language is: hit the beat with a cut, keep the frame moving with a slow zoom, and use a flash frame to reset the eye between contrasting color worlds.",
